Deezer (candidates and 30 s previews)
-------------------------------------
haystack calls Deezer's public API (https://developers.deezer.com/) for charts, editorial picks, artist radio,
related artists and 30 s previews. The previews are decoded in memory and only their vectors are kept.
Deezer's terms of use limit the API to non-commercial, private use, and Deezer may end access at any time:
https://developers.deezer.com/termsofuse. Read the Deezer notice in the README before you run the harvest.


ListenBrainz (similar recordings)
---------------------------------
The MetaBrainz Foundation. https://listenbrainz.org/
haystack calls the ListenBrainz API, within its rate limits, and sends `harvest.listenbrainz_contact` in its
User-Agent. MetaBrainz asks commercial users of its data to support it: https://metabrainz.org/supporters.


Spotify (likes, plays and the playlists)
----------------------------------------
haystack uses the Spotify Web API through your own Spotify app, under the Spotify Developer Terms
(https://developer.spotify.com/terms). It never analyses Spotify audio: taste comes from your local files and
Deezer previews.


